["https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Security/SsvcDecisionType/trackStar", "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment", "(\"Track\\*\" in the SSVC spec) The vulnerability contains specific characteristics that may require closer monitoring for changes. CISA recommends remediating Track\\* vulnerabilities within standard update timelines.", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Core/intendedUse", "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment", "A statement of how, or for what purpose, an item or artifact is intended\nto be used.", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/FunctionalSafety/RequirementVerification", "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf", "https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Core/Element", "globalId", "", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Core/ExternalIdentifierType/ecli", "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment", "[European Case Law Identifier (ECLI)](https://data.europa.eu/data/datasets/european-case-law-identifier-ecli) is a uniform identifier for judicial decisions across Europe. It consists of five mandatory components: the \"ECLI\" prefix, a country code, a court code, the year of the decision, and a unique serial number (e.g., `ECLI:EU:C:2023:94`).", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Core/RequirementStatusType/retired", "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label", "retired", "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string", "", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/FunctionalSafety/EvaluationResultType/fail", "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment", "Indicates a failed evaluation where the requirement or condition is not met.", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
